# Stone quay wall of the landings (solid): dressed limestone blocks i/m
# with d joints under a w/i coping (the walkable light lip, m/d
# underside). The top tile stands on the water line (deck row 11): its
# lower course is wet m with a T splash band at the bottom. Tiles with kai
# above are under water: the same blocks seen through clear water (T with
# b joints and t lit block tops). Open left: w lit edge; open right: d
# edge; an iron mooring ring d hangs near each open end.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grids are the source.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_kai
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
